STABLE
------
=== Adopt the `stable` pseudo-version between releases

=== Add `0.2.0--0.2.1` update script
`ALTER EXTENSION trunklet UPDATE` now works from 0.2.0. Previously there was no update path from 0.2.0.
Updated installs now also match a fresh install: the `language__get()` debug message that a fresh 0.3.3 install has is added by `0.3.3--stable` and was retroactively added to the already-released `0.3.2--0.3.3` update script.

=== Stop install and update scripts from changing the caller's settings
`CREATE EXTENSION` and `ALTER EXTENSION trunklet UPDATE` no longer change the caller's `search_path` or `client_min_messages`. Updating from 0.2.0 or 0.2.1 used to leave `search_path` at `pg_catalog`, and the install and update scripts left `client_min_messages` at `warning`.
The released `0.2.1--0.3.0` and `0.3.2--0.3.3` update scripts were edited retroactively, and so was the unreleased `0.2.0--0.2.1`. The versioned install scripts for 0.2.0 and 0.2.1 still change both settings, and the 0.3.3 install script still changes `client_min_messages` only, so `CREATE EXTENSION ... VERSION` at one of those versions does too.

0.3.3
-----
=== Add `ignore_missing_functions` agument to `template_language__remove()`
This is necessary to support properly dropping a language that was installed as
part of an extension.

0.3.2
-----
=== Fix default version in trunklet.control

0.3.1
-----
=== Mark as stable

0.3.0
-----
== Add `template_language__remove()`
This makes it possible to remove an installed template language.
